Build with -std=gnu17.

dmraid 1.0.0.rc16 passes callbacks through an unprototyped pointer,
int (*f) (), and calls it with two arguments (activate/activate.c:877).
GCC 15+ defaults to C23, where an empty parameter list means (void), so
the call and the incompatible function pointers are hard errors. The code
is fine under C17.

--- a/PKGBUILD
+++ b/PKGBUILD
@@ -33,5 +33,6 @@
 build() {
   cd "$pkgname/1.0.0.rc16-3/$pkgname"
+  export CFLAGS+=' -std=gnu17'
   ./configure --enable-led --enable-intel_led
   make -j1
 }
